---
description: Apply this rule when Cursor is reviewing an implementation diff or deciding whether the workflow is done.
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

- Cursor strong model owns the review phase.
- Explicitly apply the logic of `pr-reviewer` for correctness, regressions, and missing tests.
- Explicitly apply the logic of `review-plan-implementation` when an implementation must be checked against a plan or OpenSpec tasks.
- On security-sensitive changes, add a `best-minds` pass from a top-tier security reviewer perspective.
- Record findings in `.ai-pair/review_findings.md`.
- If any open finding is `high` or `critical`, do not mark the change `done`.
- If the issue is design drift rather than a local defect, move the phase back to `planning`.
